course: dictionary
lesson: 6949
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word painting can do more than one job. It can name a thing, name an activity, or show an action happening now. Read the words around it to find out which job it does.
explain: A painting is a picture made with paint. In «In AD 79 Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash, and it was dug out much later with streets, shops, paintings», paintings are the pictures that were found there.
explain: Painting on its own can mean the art or job of making pictures with paint. Painting can also be a verb: in «He is painting the fence», the word is shows the action is happening now. You cannot say «He is paint the fence», so you know painting is part of a verb.
fact: Painting can be a noun (a picture, or the art of making pictures) or a verb form (the -ing form of paint).
fact: A painting is a picture made with paint.
fact: The -ing form of paint is painting, as in «He is painting the fence».
fact: Look at small clue words such as is, was or were: they show that an action is going on.
fact: Test your meaning: swap in picture or art. If the sentence still makes sense, painting is a noun.
exercise: In «He is painting the fence», what job does painting do? | The name of a fence | A colour | A name for a picture | *An action he is doing now
exercise: In «some cave paintings are over 30,000 years old», what is a painting? | A kind of rock | *A picture made with paint | The art of cooking | A tall building
exercise: The Mock Turtle's joke «Fainting in Coils» sounds like which art? | Dancing | *Painting in oils | Singing | Writing
test: In «Pompeii was dug out with streets, shops and paintings», what is a painting? | *A picture | A street | A shop | A wall of a house
test: In «Rat and Mole were painting and varnishing», what is painting doing? | A name for a boat | A kind of paddle | *An action they were doing | A picture of a river
exam: In «Painting is my favourite hobby», what does painting mean? | A picture on a wall | *The art or activity of making pictures with paint | A tall building | A word for a loud noise
